## Running it

```
docker compose up -d
```

Then watch startup with `docker compose ps` and `docker compose logs -f`. SonarQube's own
readiness is exposed at `/api/system/status`; the orchestrator and Vortex each expose a
`/health` endpoint. With TLS on they publish no plain port: with `--edition none` reach them
through `agentic-proxy` on 8443 (orchestrator) and 8444 (Vortex), otherwise use `docker compose exec`.

Every long-running service reports healthy once it is ready. The init services prepare a volume
and then exit with code 0; `docker compose ps -a` lists them as exited, which is expected.

The project name above prefixes every container, network and volume. Run a second bundle of the
same edition on this host only after regenerating it with a different `--project-name`.

